## 2. Deterministic Feature Verdict Criteria (`RP3`, `RP4`, `RP7`)

Defects use strictly the unified 3-tier severity scale **`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`):

| Verdict | Mandatory Condition |
|---|---|
| **`{{accepted_word}}` (`ACCEPTED`)** | Every AC is `PASS`, all planned cases are `PASS`, and `0` open `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR` defects remain |
| **`{{changes_word}}` (`CHANGES_REQUESTED`)** | Any AC is `FAIL`, or `>= 1` open `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR` defect remains |
| **`{{blocked_word}}` (`BLOCKED`)** | Zero `FAIL` ACs and zero open `BLOCKER`/`MAJOR` defects, but `>= 1` AC or case is `BLOCKED`, `NOT_RUN`, or `UNVERIFIED` (missing environment, tool, or data evidence) |

### Non-Negotiable Honesty Rules
- `NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` **never** count as `PASS`; always report `p PASS · f FAIL · b BLOCKED · n NOT_RUN (of <total> cases)`.
- An AC is `PASS` only when **every** mapped case is `PASS`.
- Limitations (stubbed providers, unrun cases, uncovered roles/environments, flaky checks) appear in the top executive header.
- Expected results from the approved test plan are never edited inside the report; approved departures are listed under `Deviations from the Plan`.

